You've buried the lede somewhat. There probably *aren't* context-free=20
formal definitions possible for {zo'e}, because speakers usually intend=20
either the semantics of {zi'o} (pretend that the place doesn't exist) or=20
{su'o da} (something fills the place but it is irrelevant; it does=20
logically exist, though!) The former is fulfilled when zero or more objects=
=20
match, but the latter requires at least one object to match.

As a basic example, in the utterance {mi vecnu zo'e}, am I asserting that=
=20
at least one sale takes place? (Ignoring temporal issues.)

